c(1) -- Compile and execute C "scripts" in one go!
=====================================================
<!-- vim: set filetype=markdown: -->

## SYNOPSIS

`c` [OPTIONS] \<FILE.C\> [COMPILER\_FLAGS] [ARGUMENTS]

## OPTIONS

* `--clear-cache`:
  Clear compilation cache.
* `--help`:
  Print help message
* `--version`:
  Print version

## EXAMPLES

Here is a simple example:
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("Hello World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

Run it by typing:
```bash
$ c hello.c
Hello World!
```

Or, call it from the shebang!
```c
#!/usr/bin/c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("Hello World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```
```bash
$ chmod +x hello.c
$ ./hello.c
Hello World!
```
